WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.020
Hoshino Yumemi?

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.980
That's right. Hoshino Yumemi.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.990
Video feed's live!

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.320
That was the name chosen from 1263 entries.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.820
Doesn't it sound nice?

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.790
Yes, I think it is a wonderful name.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.790
Thank you very much.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.500
Don't thank us, thank our customers.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.670
Do your best out there, Yumemi!

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.880
Yes, I will do my best.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:37.600
Yumemi, we um... need to go on a trip for a while.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.020
A trip? That sounds wonderful.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:43.980
Yumemi...

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.860
Could you please wait for us here until we return?

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.320
Yes, understood. When will you be returning?

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.650
That's...

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.830
W-We're not really sure yet.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.420
But we'll be back for sure.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.710
When that happens,
let's work together again, okay?

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.460
Do you understand, Yumemi?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.380
Yes, Mr. Manager.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.790
<i>It was a sarcophagus city.</i>

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.050
<i>30 years ago, when the war was still in its infancy,</i>

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.510
<i>the city was struck by a genetically
engineered bioweapon,</i>

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.800
<i>and subsequently abandoned.</i>

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.430
These damn tin cans sure don't let up, huh?!

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.100
<i>Anti-personnel tanks still defend
their territory from intruders,</i>

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.980
<i>unaware that the city has long since been
reduced to nothing but rubble and ruins.</i>

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.710
A military installation?

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.580
<i>I was searching</i>

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.210
<i>for preserved foods,</i>

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.380
<i>medical supplies,</i>

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:14.670
<i>precision tools,</i>

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.710
<i>weapons, ammunition, and so on.</i>

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.430
<i>Anything I could use.</i>

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:24.180
<i>That was the job of those
who called themselves Junkers.</i>

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.140
Working electricity? Here?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.190
This place doesn't look military.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:34.420
Congratulations! You are our 2,500,000th customer!

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.550
<i>What the hell is a woman doing in a place like this?</i>

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.770
What do you want?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.320
I beg your pardon.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.530
I humbly, humbly beg your pardon.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.280
I was being quite dishonest.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:10.990
To be precise, you are the 2,487,288th customer.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.660
Actually, that's not entirely accurate either.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.420
Some time ago, I made an exception
and let a little boy and little girl in

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:26.630
when they didn't have enough for the admission fee.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:34.560
So technically, you are the 2,487,290th customer.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.560
I sincerely beg your pardon...

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.150
Um, Mr. Customer?

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:51.280
You are our first customer
in exactly 29 years and 81 days.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:57.250
Welcome to the rooftop planetarium
of the Flowercrest Department Store!

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.420
Are you a robot?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.210
Yes! I am a robot.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.960
My name is Hoshino Yumemi,
and I am a member of staff at this institution.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.010
What the hell is that?

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.310
It is a bouquet.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.430
Please accept this in commemoration
of your visit here.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.480
A bouquet, huh?

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.440
I beg your pardon!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.490
I was not able to acquire real flowers for you.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:31.700
My phone calls to the florist on the
first floor have not been connecting lately.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.450
So I tried making one myself.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.870
Are you malfunctioning?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.380
Yes. I am malfunctioning just slightly.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.510
There currently exists an unidentified
bug in my self-diagnostic subroutines.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:53.010
My backup CMOS battery is depleted
and must be replaced.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:57.730
My cervical vertebral power unit is past
its operational lifespan and must be replaced.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:01.190
There also exists known issues
with my personal information databases

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.980
and my conversation subroutines.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.820
Because of them, a unique characteristic
of this unit is its tendency to engage

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.990
in verbose conversation without
proper consideration of time.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.030
You gotta be kidding me...

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.780
Um, Mr. Customer?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.660
Are you perhaps not feeling well?

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.790
May I escort you to our
department store's medical office?

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.920
Mr. Customer? Mr. Customer?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.590
Shut up. I'm neither a customer, nor am I sick.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:30.800
Is that so?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.430
Well then, the next projection
will begin in seven minutes.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.470
Please take a seat and wait patiently until then.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.890
Let me repeat myself. I am <i>not</i> a customer.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:45.690
Is that so? But since you are here anyway,
by all means, please view the projection.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.650
Shut up.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.240
The projection is only 45 minutes long.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.360
Look, just shut up.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.910
Oh, and I am most sorry,
but smoking during the projection is...

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.950
Shut up! Keep your mouth shut!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.950
I'm begging you here, just stop talking!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.290
Understood. Request acknowledged.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.790
<i>My god.</i>

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:06.630
Um, Mr. Customer. There is one request
I would like to make before I stop talking.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.050
Look, your silence lasted
for all of three seconds.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.680
If it is not too much trouble, please take this.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.760
I would like you to view the special projection

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.430
reserved in commemoration
of the 2,500,000th customer.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.680
How about it?

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.190
Do whatever you want.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.860
Thank you very much.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:32.070
Well then, I shall go prepare the projection,
so please wait patiently for a while.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.570
Wait a sec.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:38.370
Is there something I can help you with?

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.830
What are you going to show me? A holovid?

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.080
The starry sky.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.330
The starry sky?

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.330
That is correct. The starry sky.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.720
The starry sky, huh?

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.230
<i>I've only got two left...</i>

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.440
What?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:17.910
Thank you all for coming to Flowercrest
Department Store's rooftop planetarium today.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:23.950
My name is Hoshino Yumemi,
and I am a member of staff at this institution.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:28.580
Before the projection begins,
I would like to announce a few important things.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:34.590
Please do not talk or whisper during the projection,
as this would be a disturbance to the other customers.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:40.760
Please turn off your cell phones and any alarms now.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:48.350
In addition, please do not eat, drink,
or smoke at any time during the projection.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.900
And finally, I would like to introduce
a most important partner

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.320
who will take you all into the world of the stars.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.160
Everyone, please welcome her
with a warm round of applause!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.160
I present to you Miss Jena!

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.830
To tell you the truth...

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.670
Miss Jena is...

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.590
the name of this big machine!

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.970
Um, Mr. Customer?

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.220
You are supposed to laugh here.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.520
You expected me to laugh?

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.860
Cut the crap and just start
the damn thing already.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:37.860
Thank you. I am very grateful
that you are anticipating it this much.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.160
Anticipating, my ass...

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:46.200
Now then, without further ado,
Miss Jena will greet you all!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.880
And once again.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.800
Miss Jena will greet you all!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.230
I thought you were gonna show me the stars.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.980
Um, Mr. Customer... I beg your pardon.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.860
I humbly, humbly beg your pardon!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.860
I am ashamed to be telling you this,

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:25.120
but it seems that our projector
is in a state of serious breakdown.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.870
Mr. Manager and the rest of the staff are on a trip,

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:32.290
and a simple unit such as myself
could not possibly grasp the situation...

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.380
Whatever. I don't give a damn.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:12:00.070
Do you know what the most irritating thing
is when venturing into that sarcophagus city?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.200
The most irritating thing in that sarcophagus city...

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.500
was, without a doubt, the time I met that robot.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:17.880
Even if it talks to you, don't respond to it.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.180
Just the bouquet. Gave me a heart attack.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.520
Looks like I was asleep for an entire day.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:42.190
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:49.030
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.290
All the stars in the sky await you.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.710
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.840
Good afternoon, Mr. Customer.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.880
How are you feeling?

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.630
Been worse. I just fell asleep, is all.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.640
<i>I guess I have about an hour before sunset...</i>

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.600
Mr. Customer, you must love the stars.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.110
What makes you think that?

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.070
You are wearing a pendant
with a constellation design.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.240
That is Cygnus, the Swan.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:24.950
This?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.330
I'll be going now. Sorry to bother you.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.660
Mr. Customer?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:35.080
If you wait 18 more minutes,
the next projection will begin.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.830
That device is broken though, right?

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:43.010
That device? Do you mean Miss Jena?

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.170
Yeah.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.800
Yes, Miss Jena is currently out of order.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:51.060
But I expect repairs to be done,
if you wait just a moment.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:54.020
Sorry, waiting's not my strong suit.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:59.230
In that case, how about shopping in our department
store while repairs are being conducted?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:02.570
There are some great discount
coupons I can print out for you.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.700
There's no one here.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.570
Who the hell's gonna fix that piece of junk?

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.620
There is no reason for concern.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.160
I have already put in a request for the repair team.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.870
They should be here soon,
and will begin repairs immediately.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.080
<i>Apparently the concept of a
rhetorical question is beyond her...</i>

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.960
Um, Mr. Customer?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.840
Could it be that you are not feeling well?

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:27.420
If that is the case, I can escort you to the medical—

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.840
Enough.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:33.140
Pardon me for asking,
but what do you mean by "Enough"?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.390
I mean, I understand.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.730
I'll be downstairs.
Call me when the repairs are done.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.190
Yes, understood.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.780
<i>Who would've thought getting out
of here would be so much trouble...</i>

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.650
Thank you very much. I am glad to hear that.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:53.490
To tell you the truth, I was quite worried
since I thought that you had become displeased

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.160
because I made a careless mistake.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:02.500
We robots take joy in serving
humans and putting you at ease.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:06.920
When the projector is repaired, I will broadcast
the news over the building's PA system.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.180
We have a special projection
prepared just for you,

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:26.190
so please don't hesitate to
remind me upon your return.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.320
Sure.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:31.240
You will be the first customer
to view the special projection.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:36.410
Every member of our staff gave
their best effort to produce it,

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:40.080
so I too, will perform my role
in this without a single mistake.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:46.000
Additionally, I will keep your bouquet
safe with the utmost care as well.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.010
I shall patiently await your return.
